| Accessibility | [WCAG 2.1 Checklist](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/) |
| Performance | [Lighthouse](https://developers.google.com/web/tools/lighthouse) |
| CI/CD | [GitHub Actions Docs](https://docs.github.com/en/actions) |

---

### Final Thought

Building a frontend for an e‑commerce site is a marathon, not a sprint.  
Start small: get a **minimum viable product** (MVP) with a handful of products, a working cart, and a checkout flow.  
Iterate, measure, and refactor.  
With the stack and workflow above, you’ll have a solid foundation that scales, stays maintainable, and delivers a great user experience.

Happy coding! 🚀
